        "independent_answer": "Stacks bottom->top: 8:[8]; 2:[8,2]; /:[4]; 3:[4,3]; -:[1]. Result 1. op2 is the most recently pushed right operand, op1 the older left operand. Reversing them changes integer 8/2=4 to 2/8=0 and changes subtraction sign.",
        "reasoning": "The evaluator interprets each nonoperator character as one operand via ch-'0'. Thus \"12 3+\" is not tokenized as 12,3,+: it interprets 1 and 2 separately and even the space as an invalid numeric offset. It needs a tokenizer and whitespace handling for multidigit expressions.",
        "evidence": [
          "docs/verify/review-overhaul-20261017/independent-answers.json",
          "docs/verify/review-overhaul-20261017/independent-delta.json",
          "docs/verify/review-overhaul-20261017/c11-result.txt"
